+# API contract v2: the Pilot slice (draft for the v1 feature lock)
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Version | 2.0 (draft) |
+| Status | For review and sign-off at the feature lock. Not implemented; both apps still run on sample data. |
+| Replaces | Nothing yet. The [full contract (v1)](/wiki/api?v=1) stays as the long-term map; v2 is what gets built first. |
+| Machine-readable form | [`openapi-v2.yaml`](openapi-v2.yaml) (OpenAPI 3.1) |
+| Last updated | 24 November 2026 |
+
+## 1 · In one minute
+
+**What v2 is.** The smallest API that lets Aurelia run its **first paid creator pilot**: 3 to 5 creators each sell a retreat ticket to their audience, buyers sign up, build and play sessions, check in before and after, and some move on to Plus. Everything the pilot does not need waits.
+
+**What changed since v1, and why.** The v1 contract described the whole product: community, challenges, coins, invites and 18 admin modules, built in five phases. Since then four decisions changed what the backend must serve first:
+
+- **The business needs a paid pilot before the whole product.** So v2 is one "Pilot slice" phase after Foundation, not P0 to P4.
+- **The creator retreat was redesigned and approved.** A one-off ticket (€19.99 or €39), Aurelia as the seller (merchant of record), a 70/30 split paid to creators in money, plus a share of the Plus revenue each cohort brings. That needs one-off payments and Stripe Connect payouts, which the backend plan wanted to retire. v2 keeps them.
+- **Safety cannot wait for the last phase.** People type how they feel into free text, so crisis messages are certain. The safety check, the crisis response and the safety log are part of the core loop.
+- **The business wants to know what moving someone from a bad state to a good one costs, and whether it works.** Every build now records what it bought from which AI supplier and at what cost (the compute ledger), and every chapter records a check-in score before and after (therapeutic outcomes). This is internal measurement, aggregate only, never public claims.
+
+**The rule: features are locked before the final API.** Every feature that stores data costs an endpoint, a table, backend logic with tests, and changes in both apps. So:
+
+1. The product owner and the business owner sign off a one-page list of what API v1 serves (this slice, plus anything agreed) **before** engineering plans the final API.
+2. A change after the lock first gets an **impact note** from engineering (endpoints, tables, screens, days added). Then the product owner decides.
+3. Once live, the API changes by **versions, not edits**: new fields and endpoints are added; anything breaking goes to the next version.
+4. The prototype may keep moving on sample data. The API does not.
+
+## 2 · How the pieces fit
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+  W[Web app] --> API[Aurelia API v1]
+  F[Flutter app] --> API
+  A[Admin] --> API
+  API --> B[Backend services]
+  B --> DB[(PostgreSQL)]
+  B --> Q[Job queue and workers]
+  Q --> AI[AI suppliers: script, voice, music, image]
+  Q --> OS[Object storage for audio]
+  B --> S[Stripe: payments and Connect payouts]
+  S -->|webhooks| API
+  B --> L[Compute ledger and outcomes]
+  L --> DB
+```
+
+| Piece | What it is | Today |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| The apps (web, Flutter, admin) | What people see and tap | Built, on sample data |
+| The API | The list of questions the apps may ask, and the exact shape of each answer | This document |
+| The backend | Stores accounts and check-ins, runs the AI, takes payments, keeps data safe | Not built for 2026 |
+| Database and suppliers | PostgreSQL, AI models (script, voice, music, image), object storage, Stripe | Chosen, not set up |
+
+All AI runs on the server. The apps never hold a model key or a payment secret.
+
+## 3 · Conventions
+
+Carried from v1 (§3 there), trimmed to what the slice uses.
+
+- **Base path** `https://api.aurelia.care/v1` (staging `https://api.staging.aurelia.care/v1`). The API's own first version is `/v1`; "contract v2" is the second draft of the document, not a `/v2` path.
+- **JSON, camelCase** field names, RFC 3339 UTC timestamps, durations in seconds, money as **integer minor units with a currency** (`{ amount: 1999, currency: "EUR" }`).
+- **Ids** are opaque strings with a type prefix: `usr_`, `cns_`, `cnv_`, `msg_`, `bld_`, `ses_`, `chp_`, `ver_`, `bit_`, `ply_`, `chk_`, `jrn_`, `crt_`, `ret_`, `coh_`, `enr_`, `ord_`, `ref_`, `spl_`, `pay_`, `sub_`, `cmp_`, `sfe_`, `aud_`.
+- **Auth:** `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>`, 15-minute access token; an opaque rotating refresh token (30 days rolling) in an httpOnly cookie on web and secure storage on mobile. Roles: `user`, `creator`, and staff roles on a separate admin audience (`aud: admin`).
+- **Errors:** RFC 9457 problem details with a stable `code` the apps switch on, and `retryable`. Codes used by the slice: `invalid_request` (400), `unauthenticated` (401), `forbidden` (403), `not_found` (404), `conflict`, `build_in_progress`, `already_enrolled` (409), `unsafe_content`, `consent_required`, `age_restricted`, `withdrawal_consent_required` (422), `rate_limited`, `build_limit_reached` (429), `ai_unavailable`, `payment_unavailable` (503).
+- **Pagination:** cursor, `?limit=20&cursor=…` → `{ data: T[], nextCursor: string | null }`, `limit` ≤ 100.
+- **Idempotency-Key** (a UUID) is **required** on every payment, refund, build, check-in and message POST; webhook handlers deduplicate on the supplier's event id. A replay returns the first result for 24 h.
+- **Rate limits** per token: 60 requests/min general, 20 messages/min, 10 builds/hour, 5 checkouts/hour. `RateLimit-*` headers; `Retry-After` on 429.
+- **Streaming:** Server-Sent Events for the assistant's reply and a build's progress. Streams end with a terminal event; the resource fetched by id is always the truth.
+- **Versioning:** additive changes (new fields, new enum values) are not breaking; apps ignore unknown fields and treat unknown enum values as "other". Breaking changes need a new path version.
+- **Headers:** `Aurelia-Client: web/<version>+<commit>` or `ios/…`, `android/…` on every request.
+
+**Status labels below:** **v1** = in the v1 contract as it was; **changed in v2** = in v1, with a different shape or rule; **new in v2** = not in v1.
+
+## 4 · The Pilot slice, area by area
+
+Shapes are TypeScript-like. `?` is optional. Auth: **public**, **user**, **creator**, **staff**, **Stripe** (signature).
+
+### 4.1 Accounts and consent (12 endpoints)
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose | Request → Response | Auth | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/auth/signup` | Create an account with email and password | `{ email, password, name, birthYear, country, acceptTermsVersion }` → `AuthTokens & { user: Me }` | public | changed in v2 (age gate, country) |
+| POST | `/auth/signin` | Sign in | `{ email, password }` → `AuthTokens & { user: Me }` | public | v1 |
+| POST | `/auth/oauth/google` | Sign up or in with Google; the code exchange runs on the server | `{ code, redirectUri, birthYear?, country? }` → `AuthTokens & { user: Me, needsAgeGate: boolean }` | public | v1 (Google only in the slice) |
+| POST | `/auth/refresh` | Swap the refresh token for a new pair | cookie or `{ refreshToken }` → `AuthTokens` | public | v1 |
+| POST | `/auth/signout` | Revoke the refresh token | — → `204` | user | v1 |
+| POST | `/auth/password-reset` | Ask for a reset link; never reveals whether the address exists | `{ email }` → `202` | public | v1 |
+| GET | `/me` | The signed-in person | → `Me` | user | v1 |
+| PATCH | `/me` | Name, locale, time zone, birth year (once) | `Partial<{ name, locale, timeZone, birthYear }>` → `Me` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/me/consents` | Every consent and its state | → `{ data: Consent[] }` | user | changed in v2 (purposes below) |
+| PUT | `/me/consents/{purpose}` | Give or withdraw one consent | `{ granted: boolean, textVersion }` → `Consent` | user | changed in v2 |
+| POST | `/me/export` | Ask for a copy of all one's data (GDPR access) | — → `202 { requestId, readyBy }` | user | v1 |
+| DELETE | `/me` | Delete the account and its data (30-day grace, then gone) | `{ confirm: "DELETE" }` → `202 { deleteAt }` | user | v1 |
+
+```ts
+type AuthTokens = { accessToken: string; expiresIn: number; refreshToken?: string } // refreshToken only to mobile
+type Me = { id: string; email: string; name: string; locale: string; timeZone: string;
+            country: string; ageBand: "16-17" | "18+"; roles: ("user" | "creator")[]; createdAt: string }
+type Consent = { purpose: "health_data" | "ai_processing" | "outcome_research" | "marketing_email";
+                 granted: boolean; textVersion: string; updatedAt: string }
+```
+
+**Age gate.** Sign-up asks for a birth year. Under 16 is refused (`422 age_restricted`); 16 and 17 get the account with marketing off and stricter safety thresholds. Google sign-in without a birth year returns `needsAgeGate: true` and the app asks before anything else.
+
+**Consent.** `health_data` (explicit, GDPR Art. 9) is required before the first check-in or free-text feeling is stored; without it those calls return `422 consent_required`. `outcome_research` lets the person's scores count in internal aggregate outcomes; it is separate and optional. Consent texts are versioned; a new text version re-asks.
+
+### 4.2 Core loop (22 endpoints)
+
+The loop: a check-in score before → a conversation → a build creates a session with chapters → play → a check-in score after → "Change this session" with Lego bites makes a new version → the next chapter, inside a journey from a bad state toward a good one.
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose | Request → Response | Auth | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/conversations` | Start a thread, optionally from the first sentence | `{ firstMessage?, source }` → `Conversation` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/conversations` | My threads | → `Page<Conversation>` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/conversations/{id}` | One thread with its messages | → `Conversation & { messages: Message[] }` | user | v1 |
+| POST | `/conversations/{id}/messages` | Send a message; the reply streams (SSE) | `{ text }` → `text/event-stream`: `message.delta`, `message.completed`, `safety.crisis`, `error` | user | v1, safety now blocking |
+| POST | `/builds` | Build a new session or a new version of one | `{ conversationId, sessionId?, baseVersionId?, chapterMinutes: 3 \| 5 \| 10, biteIds?: string[] }` → `202 Build` | user | changed in v2 (bites, chapter length) |
+| GET | `/builds/{id}` | Build state | → `Build` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/builds/{id}/events` | Build progress (SSE) | → `build.step`, `build.completed`, `build.failed` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/sessions` | My sessions (created and played) | `?filter=created\|played` → `Page<SessionSummary>` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/sessions/{id}` | One session with its current version | → `Session` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/sessions/{id}/chapters` | The chapters of the current (or a given) version | `?versionId` → `{ data: Chapter[] }` | user | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/sessions/{id}/versions` | Every version, newest first | → `{ data: Version[] }` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/sessions/{id}/bites` | "Change this session": the Lego bites on offer for this version, each with a Why | → `{ data: LegoBite[] }` | user | new in v2 (replaces v1 proposals) |
+| POST | `/sessions/{id}/versions/{versionId}/rollback` | Make an earlier version current again (no cost) | — → `Session` | user | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/chapters/{id}/playback` | Signed, short-lived audio and image URLs | → `Playback` | user | v1 (per chapter now) |
+| POST | `/plays` | A play starts | `{ chapterId, versionId }` → `Play` | user | changed in v2 |
+| PATCH | `/plays/{id}` | Progress and end of a play | `{ positionSec, completionRatio, ended?: boolean, report?: "adverse" \| "quality" }` → `Play` | user | changed in v2 (completion ratio, report) |
+| POST | `/checkins` | A pre- or post-session score | `{ chapterId?, journeyId?, phase: "pre" \| "post", score: 0-100, feeling?: string }` → `CheckIn` | user | changed in v2 (pre and post, 0–100) |
+| GET | `/checkins` | My check-ins | `?journeyId` → `Page<CheckIn>` | user | v1 |
+| POST | `/journeys` | Start a journey from a bad state toward a good one | `{ domain, fromState, toState, startScore, targetScore? }` → `Journey` | user | changed in v2 |
+| GET | `/journeys/current` | The active journey and its next chapter | → `Journey \| null` | user | v1 |
+| GET | `/journeys/{id}` | One journey with its scores | → `Journey` | user | changed in v2 |
+| PATCH | `/journeys/{id}` | Pause, resume or end | `{ status }` → `Journey` | user | v1 |
+
+```ts
+type Conversation = { id; sessionId: string | null; title; source: "home" | "onboarding" | "retreat" | "session" | "new"; lastMessageAt }
+type Message = { id; conversationId; role: "user" | "assistant" | "system_event"; text; createdAt;
+                 attachment?: { type: "bites"; sessionId } | { type: "build"; buildId; versionId; label };
+                 safety?: { crisis: boolean } }
+type Build = { id; sessionId; versionId; state: "queued" | "running" | "ready" | "failed";
+               steps: { name: "script" | "voice" | "music" | "image" | "mix"; state }[];
+               reusedSegments: number;            // "produced once, personalised inserts"
+               counted: boolean; createdAt; finishedAt? }
+type Session = { id; title; summary; ownerId; retreatId?: string; currentVersionId; versions: number; createdAt }
+type Version = { id; sessionId; label: "v1.0"; parentVersionId?: string; biteIds: string[];
+                 state: "building" | "ready" | "failed" | "rolled_back"; createdAt }
+type Chapter = { id; versionId; index; title; durationSec; minutes: 3 | 5 | 10 }
+type LegoBite = { id; title; kind: "voice" | "music" | "pace" | "script" | "image" | "length";
+                  what: string; why: string; preselected: boolean }
+type Playback = { audioUrl; imageUrl?; expiresAt; durationSec }   // URLs live 15 minutes
+type Play = { id; chapterId; versionId; startedAt; positionSec; completionRatio: number; completed: boolean }
+type CheckIn = { id; phase: "pre" | "post"; score: number; chapterId?; journeyId?; createdAt }
+type Journey = { id; domain: "sleep" | "stress" | "focus" | "mood" | "other"; fromState; toState;
+                 startScore; targetScore; latestScore?; chaptersPlayed; status: "active" | "paused" | "flipped" | "ended";
+                 nextChapterId?; reminderAt? }
+```
+
+**Rules the server owns.**
+- A build is refused while another build of the same session runs (`409 build_in_progress`).
+- Applying bites always makes a **new version**; the previous one is kept. Closing the sheet without applying costs nothing.
+- A play with `completionRatio` below 0.3 never counts as complete.
+- An `adverse` report on a play rolls the session back to the previous version and writes a safety event.
+- A missing post score stays `null`; the server never fills it in.
+- `targetScore` defaults to 75. A journey is **flipped** when a post score reaches the target on two chapters in a row (internal definition, see §4.7).
+
+### 4.3 Safety (2 endpoints, plus a check inside every text endpoint)
+
+Safety is **P1**, inside the core loop.
+
+- **Every user text** (a message, a first sentence, a check-in's `feeling`, a retreat intake) passes a mandatory safety check **before** any generation. There is no endpoint for it; it is part of those calls.
+- On a **crisis** signal the server stops generation, does not build, returns the reply as `safety.crisis` (or `422 unsafe_content` on non-streaming calls) with local crisis resources, and writes a `safety_events` row. A creator persona can never override this.
+- Every safety event has a named **escalation owner** (open decision, §8) and appears in the admin (§4.8).
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose | Request → Response | Auth | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/safety/resources` | Crisis lines for a country | `?country=ID` → `{ data: { name, phone?, url?, hours? }[] }` | public | new in v2 |
+| POST | `/safety/reports` | Report a reply or a session as harmful | `{ messageId? , chapterId?, reason, note? }` → `202` | user | new in v2 |
+
+```ts
+type CrisisReply = { code: "unsafe_content"; category: "self_harm" | "harm_to_others" | "medical_emergency";
+                     message: string; resources: { name; phone?; url? }[] }
+```
+
+### 4.4 Creator retreat (17 endpoints)
+
+The approved redesign: a creator sells a retreat (a journey produced once in the creator's voice, with short personal inserts per buyer) to a **cohort**. **Aurelia is the merchant of record**: it sells the ticket, charges VAT, handles refunds and the EU withdrawal right, and pays the creator through Stripe Connect.
+
+**The split** (default, per retreat in `split_rules`): of the ticket's net after VAT and card fees, **70% to the creator, 30% to Aurelia**; plus a **share of year-1 Plus revenue** (proposed 20%) from buyers in the creator's cohorts who subscribe within the attribution window. Ticket price €19.99 or €39.
+
+**Creators see aggregates only.** No names, no scores, no feelings. Cohort numbers are hidden for any group smaller than the minimum group size (proposed 10; below it the response says `suppressed: true`).
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose | Request → Response | Auth | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/creators/{handle}` | A creator's public page | → `CreatorPublic` | public | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/retreats/{id}` | A retreat's public page and its open cohorts | → `Retreat & { cohorts: Cohort[] }` | public | new in v2 |
+| POST | `/checkout/tickets` | Start a ticket purchase (Stripe Checkout) | `{ cohortId, withdrawalConsent: { startNow: true, acknowledged: true, textVersion }? }` → `{ orderId, checkoutUrl }` | user | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/orders/{id}` | One order and its state | → `Order` | user | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/me/orders` | My orders | → `Page<Order>` | user | new in v2 |
+| POST | `/orders/{id}/withdrawal` | Use the 14-day withdrawal right, if it still applies | `{ reason? }` → `Refund` | user | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/me/enrolments` | My retreats and where I am in each | → `{ data: Enrolment[] }` | user | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/creator/me` | The creator's own profile and payout status | → `Creator` | creator | new in v2 |
+| POST | `/creator/connect/onboarding-link` | A Stripe Connect onboarding link | — → `{ url, expiresAt }` | creator | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/creator/retreats` | The creator's retreats and cohorts | → `{ data: (Retreat & { cohorts: Cohort[] })[] }` | creator | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/creator/cohorts/{id}/metrics` | Aggregate cohort numbers | → `CohortMetrics` | creator | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/creator/payouts` | The creator's payout ledger | → `Page<PayoutLine>` | creator | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/creator/split-rules` | The terms that apply to each retreat | → `{ data: SplitRule[] }` | creator | new in v2 |
+| POST | `/admin/creators` | Onboard a creator (pilot: by hand) | `{ userId, handle, displayName, country }` → `Creator` | staff | new in v2 |
+| POST | `/admin/retreats` | Create a retreat with its price and split | `{ creatorId, title, priceAmount, currency, splitRuleId, chapterPlan }` → `Retreat` | staff | new in v2 |
+| POST | `/admin/retreats/{id}/cohorts` | Open a cohort | `{ startsAt, capacity, enrolUntil }` → `Cohort` | staff | new in v2 |
+| PUT | `/admin/split-rules/{id}` | Set or change a split (new version, never an edit in place) | `{ creatorTicketShare, creatorPlusShare, plusAttributionDays }` → `SplitRule` | staff | new in v2 |
+
+```ts
+type Money = { amount: number; currency: "EUR" | "USD" | "IDR" }
+type Retreat = { id; creatorId; title; summary; price: Money; weeks: number; chapterCount; status: "draft" | "on_sale" | "closed" }
+type Cohort = { id; retreatId; startsAt; enrolUntil; capacity; enrolled: number; status: "open" | "running" | "finished" }
+type Order = { id; userId; cohortId; price: Money; vat: Money; fees: Money; net: Money;
+               state: "pending" | "paid" | "refunded" | "partially_refunded" | "failed";
+               withdrawal: { waived: boolean; consentAt?: string; textVersion?: string };
+               receiptUrl?; createdAt }
+type Enrolment = { id; cohortId; retreatId; orderId; journeyId; status: "active" | "finished" | "refunded" }
+type SplitRule = { id; version: number; creatorTicketShare: 0.7; creatorPlusShare: 0.2; plusAttributionDays: 365; effectiveFrom }
+type PayoutLine = { id; creatorId; source: "ticket" | "plus_share" | "refund_reversal"; orderId?; subscriptionId?;
+                    gross: Money; creatorAmount: Money; state: "pending" | "available" | "paid" | "reversed";
+                    stripeTransferId?; availableAt; paidAt? }
+type CohortMetrics = { cohortId; minGroupSize: number; suppressed: boolean; enrolled?: number;
+                       activeWeek1?: number; activeWeek4?: number; activeWeek8?: number;
+                       chaptersPlayedMedian?: number; plusConversions?: number; refunds?: number;
+                       revenue?: Money; creatorEarnings?: Money }   // never per-person data
+```
+
+**Withdrawal.** For EU buyers, checkout refuses to start an instantly-delivered retreat without the express consent to start now and the acknowledgement that the right is then lost (`422 withdrawal_consent_required`). Without that consent the buyer keeps the 14-day right and access starts at the cohort start. The confirmation goes out by email (a durable medium).
+
+**Payouts.** A paid order writes a `pending` payout line; it becomes `available` after the refund window, then a scheduled transfer pays it through Stripe Connect. A refund after payout writes a `refund_reversal` line against the creator's next payout.
+
+### 4.5 Plus subscription (6 endpoints)
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose | Request → Response | Auth | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/plans` | Plans and prices for the person's country | → `{ data: Plan[] }` | public | v1 |
+| POST | `/checkout/subscription` | Start Plus (Stripe Checkout on web; store billing on mobile later) | `{ planId, priceId }` → `{ checkoutUrl }` | user | changed in v2 (cohort attribution) |
+| POST | `/me/subscription/portal` | Manage or cancel (Stripe customer portal) | — → `{ url }` | user | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/me/entitlements` | What the plan allows and how much is left | → `Entitlements` | user | v1 |
+| POST | `/webhooks/stripe` | Payments, subscriptions, refunds and Connect events | Stripe event → `200` | Stripe | changed in v2 (tickets and Connect) |
+| GET | `/me/subscription` | The current subscription | → `Subscription \| null` | user | v1 |
+
+```ts
+type Plan = { id: "free" | "plus"; prices: { id; interval: "month" | "year"; price: Money }[]; limits: Limits }
+type Entitlements = { plan: "free" | "plus"; source: "free" | "subscription" | "retreat";
+                      limit: { unit: "build"; perDay: number; used: number; resetAt } ; // unit is an open decision (§8)
+                      chapterMinutesAllowed: (3 | 5 | 10)[] }
+type Subscription = { id; plan: "plus"; interval; status: "active" | "past_due" | "canceled"; currentPeriodEnd;
+                      attributedCohortId?: string }   // drives the creator's Plus share
+```
+
+**Free limit.** The server counts; the app only shows `entitlements`. The first build never counts. A retreat ticket grants its own chapters for the cohort's length (`source: "retreat"`).
+
+**Attribution.** A subscription started by someone enrolled in a cohort within `plusAttributionDays` of enrolment records `attributedCohortId`. Each paid invoice then writes a `plus_share` payout line.
+
+### 4.6 Compute ledger and cost (5 endpoints)
+
+Every build writes one ledger row **per supplier call**: what was bought, from whom, how much, at what cost, and whether a cached or reused segment made it free. This is how the business sees what a chapter, a session and a journey cost, and how that falls over time.
+
+There is no public write endpoint: the build workers write the ledger. The reads are admin only.
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose | Request → Response | Auth | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/admin/compute/ledger` | Raw ledger rows | `?from&to&media&supplier&buildId&cursor` → `Page<ComputeLine>` | staff | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/admin/compute/summary` | Cost per chapter, session, journey; by media, supplier, chapter length | `?from&to&groupBy=media\|supplier\|model\|chapterMinutes\|day` → `CostSummary` | staff | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/admin/builds/{id}/cost` | One build's cost breakdown | → `{ buildId; total: Money; lines: ComputeLine[] }` | staff | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/admin/suppliers` | Suppliers, models and their current unit prices | → `{ data: SupplierEndpoint[] }` | staff | new in v2 |
+| PUT | `/admin/suppliers/{id}` | Update a unit price or switch a supplier off (versioned) | `{ unitPrice, active }` → `SupplierEndpoint` | staff | new in v2 |
+
+```ts
+type ComputeLine = { id; buildId; chapterId?; versionId; media: "script" | "voice" | "music" | "image" | "video";
+                     supplier: string; model: string; unit: "token_in" | "token_out" | "char" | "second" | "image" | "generation";
+                     units: number; unitPrice: number; cost: Money; cacheHit: boolean; reused: boolean;
+                     latencyMs: number; attempt: number; fallbackFrom?: string; createdAt }
+type CostSummary = { from; to; groupBy; rows: { key: string; builds: number; chapters: number; cost: Money;
+                     costPerChapter: Money; cacheHitRate: number }[] }
+```
+
+Video is in the enum but not generated in the pilot.
+
+### 4.7 Therapeutic outcomes (3 endpoints, internal)
+
+Internal metric names; **never** public or partner copy, which stays wellness. Aggregate only, only from people who gave `outcome_research` consent, and suppressed below the minimum group size.
+
+- **State-flip journey:** a journey from a bad state to a good one (for example bad sleep to good sleep), with a start score, a target, the chapters played and whether it **flipped**.
+- **Uplift per chapter:** post score minus pre score on the same chapter.
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose | Request → Response | Auth | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/admin/outcomes/journeys` | Flip rate, chapters to flip, cost per flip | `?domain&from&to&retreatId` → `FlipSummary` | staff | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/admin/outcomes/uplift` | Average uplift per chapter, by chapter index, length or bite | `?domain&groupBy=chapterIndex\|chapterMinutes\|bite` → `UpliftSummary` | staff | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/admin/cohorts/{id}/metrics` | A cohort's aggregates (the creator's view, plus cost) | → `CohortMetrics & { cost: Money; flipRate?: number }` | staff | new in v2 |
+
+```ts
+type FlipSummary = { n: number; suppressed: boolean; flipRate?: number; chaptersToFlipMedian?: number;
+                     costPerFlip?: Money; startScoreMedian?: number }
+type UpliftSummary = { n: number; rows: { key: string; n: number; upliftMean?: number; suppressed: boolean }[] }
+```
+
+### 4.8 Minimum admin (9 endpoints)
+
+Staff accounts only, separate token audience, roles `super_admin`, `ops`, `moderator`, `analyst`. **Every mutation writes the audit log.** This closes the admin's missing authentication.
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose | Request → Response | Auth | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/admin/users` | Find users | `?q&plan&status&cursor` → `Page<AdminUser>` | staff | v1 |
+| GET | `/admin/users/{id}` | One user: account, orders, subscription, safety events (no check-in content) | → `AdminUser & {…}` | staff | v1 |
+| PATCH | `/admin/users/{id}` | Suspend or reactivate | `{ status, reason }` → `AdminUser` | staff | v1 |
+| GET | `/admin/transactions` | Orders, subscriptions, refunds, payouts | `?type&from&to&cursor` → `Page<Transaction>` | staff | changed in v2 |
+| POST | `/admin/orders/{id}/refunds` | Refund all or part of an order | `{ amount?: Money, reason }` → `Refund` | staff | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/admin/payouts` | Creator payouts and their state | `?creatorId&state` → `Page<PayoutLine>` | staff | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/admin/safety/events` | Safety events, newest first | `?severity&state&cursor` → `Page<SafetyEvent>` | staff | new in v2 (moved up from the last phase) |
+| PATCH | `/admin/safety/events/{id}` | Acknowledge, escalate or close | `{ state: "acknowledged" \| "escalated" \| "closed", note }` → `SafetyEvent` | staff | new in v2 |
+| GET | `/admin/audit` | The audit log | `?actor&action&from&to` → `Page<AuditEntry>` | staff | v1 |
+
+AI spend lives in §4.6 and cohort metrics in §4.7; both count as admin.
+
+```ts
+type SafetyEvent = { id; userId; source: "message" | "checkin" | "intake" | "report" | "play";
+                     category; severity: "low" | "high" | "crisis"; action: "blocked" | "resources_shown" | "rolled_back";
+                     state: "open" | "acknowledged" | "escalated" | "closed"; ownerId?; createdAt }
+type AuditEntry = { id; actorId; action: string; target: string; before?: object; after?: object; at }
+```
+
+### Endpoint count
+
+| Area | Endpoints |
+| --- | --- |
+| Accounts and consent | 12 |
+| Core loop | 22 |
+| Safety | 2 |
+| Creator retreat | 17 |
+| Plus subscription | 6 |
+| Compute ledger and cost | 5 |
+| Therapeutic outcomes | 3 |
+| Minimum admin | 9 |
+| **Total** | **76** |
+
+## 5 · Data model (PostgreSQL)
+
+UUID-backed ids with the prefixes above; `created_at` and `updated_at` on every table; money as `bigint` minor units plus `char(3)` currency. Health data (check-ins, feelings, messages) sits in its own schema with stricter access and is never joined into creator views.
+
+| Table | Key fields | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `users` | id, email (unique), password_hash?, name, birth_year, country, locale, time_zone, status, deleted_at | Age band derived from birth year |
+| `auth_identities` | user_id, provider, provider_user_id (unique pair) | Google in the slice |
+| `refresh_tokens` | id, user_id, hash, family_id, expires_at, revoked_at | Rotation with reuse detection |
+| `consents` | user_id, purpose, granted, text_version, updated_at | Append-only history in `consent_events` |
+| `consent_events` | user_id, purpose, granted, text_version, at, ip_country | Proof of consent |
+| `data_requests` | id, user_id, kind (export, delete), state, ready_at | GDPR requests |
+| `conversations` | id, user_id, session_id?, source, title | |
+| `messages` | id, conversation_id, role, text, safety_flag, attachment jsonb | Health schema |
+| `sessions` | id, owner_id, retreat_id?, title, summary, current_version_id | |
+| `session_versions` | id, session_id, label, parent_version_id?, bite_ids, state, build_id | Rollback flips `current_version_id` |
+| `chapters` | id, version_id, index, minutes, duration_sec, audio_key, image_key, segment_ids | Segments may be reused across buyers |
+| `media_segments` | id, retreat_id?, kind, object_key, hash | "Produced once": shared creator-voice segments |
+| `lego_bites` | id, kind, title, what, why, params jsonb, active | The catalogue of changes |
+| `builds` | id, session_id, version_id, user_id, state, counted, idempotency_key (unique), started_at, finished_at | |
+| `compute_ledger` | id, build_id, chapter_id?, media, supplier, model, unit, units, unit_price, cost, currency, cache_hit, reused, latency_ms, attempt, fallback_from | One row per supplier call; append-only |
+| `supplier_endpoints` | id, supplier, model, media, unit, unit_price, active, valid_from | Versioned prices |
+| `plays` | id, user_id, chapter_id, version_id, started_at, position_sec, completion_ratio, completed, report | Complete only at ≥ 0.3 |
+| `checkins` | id, user_id, journey_id?, chapter_id?, phase (pre, post), score (0–100), feeling? | Health schema |
+| `journeys` | id, user_id, domain, from_state, to_state, start_score, target_score, status, flipped_at? | State-flip journeys |
+| `therapeutic_outcomes` | id, journey_id, chapter_id, pre_score, post_score, uplift, consented | Derived per chapter; only with `outcome_research` consent |
+| `safety_events` | id, user_id, source, source_id, category, severity, action, state, owner_id, escalated_at | Kept even after account deletion, de-identified |
+| `creators` | id, user_id, handle (unique), display_name, country, stripe_account_id, payouts_enabled | |
+| `retreats` | id, creator_id, title, price_amount, currency, split_rule_id, weeks, status | |
+| `cohorts` | id, retreat_id, starts_at, enrol_until, capacity, status | |
+| `enrolments` | id, cohort_id, user_id, order_id, journey_id, status | Unique (cohort_id, user_id) |
+| `orders` | id, user_id, cohort_id, amount, vat, fees, net, currency, state, stripe_payment_intent_id, withdrawal_waived, withdrawal_consent_at, withdrawal_text_version, idempotency_key | Aurelia is merchant of record |
+| `refunds` | id, order_id, amount, reason, state, stripe_refund_id, actor_id | |
+| `split_rules` | id, version, creator_ticket_share, creator_plus_share, plus_attribution_days, effective_from | Never edited in place |
+| `payout_ledger` | id, creator_id, source, order_id?, subscription_invoice_id?, gross, creator_amount, state, available_at, stripe_transfer_id?, paid_at? | Append-only; reversals are new rows |
+| `subscriptions` | id, user_id, plan, interval, status, current_period_end, stripe_subscription_id, attributed_cohort_id? | |
+| `usage_counters` | user_id, day, builds_used | Free-limit counter |
+| `webhook_events` | id (supplier event id, unique), source, type, received_at, processed_at, error? | Deduplication |
+| `staff_users` | id, email, role, status | Admin audience |
+| `audit_log` | id, actor_id, action, target, before jsonb, after jsonb, at | Append-only |
+| `idempotency_keys` | key, user_id, route, response_hash, created_at | 24 h replay |
+
+## 6 · Webhooks and events
+
+**Inbound** (to the API):
+
+| Source | Event | What the server does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Stripe | `checkout.session.completed` (ticket) | Order → paid; enrolment, journey and pending payout line created; receipt and withdrawal confirmation emailed |
+| Stripe | `checkout.session.completed` (subscription), `invoice.paid` | Subscription active; entitlements updated; `plus_share` payout line if attributed |
+| Stripe | `customer.subscription.updated` / `.deleted` | Status and entitlements updated |
+| Stripe | `charge.refunded` | Refund row; enrolment refunded; payout reversal line |
+| Stripe Connect | `account.updated` | `payouts_enabled` on the creator |
+| Stripe Connect | `transfer.created`, `payout.failed` | Payout line → paid, or flagged in admin |
+
+Every handler verifies the Stripe signature, deduplicates on the event id in `webhook_events`, and is safe to replay.
+
+**Internal events** (queue topics, not public): `build.completed`, `build.failed`, `checkin.created`, `journey.flipped`, `safety.flagged` (pages the escalation owner when severity is `crisis`), `order.paid`, `payout.due`. Outbound partner webhooks are out of v2.
+
+## 7 · Explicitly out of v2 (later)
+
+| Out | Why it waits |
+| --- | --- |
+| Community: publish, recreate, shelves, creator follow | Not needed to sell or deliver a retreat |
+| Challenges, coins, wallet, invites | The economy follows the pilot's results |
+| Most admin modules (moderation queue, AI policy console, experiments, notifications broadcast, signal sources, compliance dashboard) | The pilot runs by hand; the slice keeps only §4.8 |
+| Wearables and signal sources (Apple Health, Whoop, Oura) | Check-in scores are enough to measure the pilot |
+| Healing Map and the learning graph (Causal AI reinforcement, pruning, tournaments) | Needs real outcomes first; the ledger and outcomes tables collect them |
+| Insurer, employer and clinical reporting | A separate regulatory track |
+| Apple sign-in, store billing on mobile | Web checkout first; Apple sign-in becomes required when the iOS app offers Google |
+| Video generation | Cost (37% of measured 2025 spend) for little gain |
+| Voice input, push notifications, outbound webhooks | After the pilot |
+
+## 8 · Open decisions before the lock
+
+| Decision | Options on the table | Blocks |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Price anchors | Retreat ticket €19.99 or €39; Plus $10 a month or $100 a year; the cost model's $19.99 per flip | Plans, checkout, the split examples |
+| Free-limit unit | Builds per day (v1), chapters, or minutes of audio | Entitlements, usage counters |
+| First pilot market | EU (withdrawal, VAT, GDPR) or Indonesia | Currencies, VAT, crisis lines, data region |
+| Safety escalation owner | A named person or rota who receives crisis events, with hours and a backup | Going live at all |
+| Data region | EU only, or EU plus a second region for Indonesia | Hosting, suppliers, the DPIA |
+| Minimum group size | 10 (proposed) or 5 | Creator and admin aggregates |
+| Creator share of Plus | 20% of year-1 Plus (proposed), and the attribution window | Split rules, payouts |
+| One voice supplier and one fallback | From the cost model's shortlist | Build pipeline, ledger prices |
+
+## 9 · Change from v1
+
+| | What | Detail |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| **Moved** | Safety | From the last phase (admin monitoring) into the core loop: blocking check, crisis reply, events, escalation |
+| **Moved** | Phasing | P0 to P4 → Foundation, then one Pilot slice; the rest after the pilot |
+| **Moved** | One-off payments, Stripe Connect | Kept for the creator retreat instead of retired |
+| **Changed** | Proposals | "Change this session" is now a list of Lego bites; applying makes a new version, with rollback |
+| **Changed** | Sessions | Chapters (3, 5 or 10 minutes) inside versions; playback per chapter |
+| **Changed** | Check-ins | A pre and a post score from 0 to 100 on each chapter |
+| **Changed** | Journeys | Start score, target and a flipped state |
+| **Changed** | Plays | Completion ratio and an adverse report |
+| **Changed** | Sign-up | Age gate and country |
+| **Added** | Creator retreat | Creators, retreats, cohorts, enrolments, ticket orders, withdrawal consent, split rules, payout ledger, refunds, Plus attribution, cohort aggregates |
+| **Added** | Compute ledger | Per supplier call: media, supplier, model, units, cost, cache hit, reuse, latency |
+| **Added** | Therapeutic outcomes | Flip rate, chapters to flip, uplift per chapter, aggregate only |
+| **Added** | Feature lock | Changes after the lock need an impact note and a decision |
+| **Dropped from the first build** | Community, challenges, coins, wallet, invites, signal sources, notifications, studies, most admin modules, Apple sign-in, store billing, video | Still in the [v1 contract](/wiki/api?v=1) as the long-term map |
+
